Kind: ablation
Issue: #978
Takes out: driver_dma_alloc()'s check of the buffer against `reach', the highest address the device can use.  On entry 70 every IOVA is from 4 GiB up, and edu_probe asks a buffer within edu's default 28 bits: given it anyway, at 0x100001000, it must say WRONG, where libdriver gave it back and refused it.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 70 600 -smp 4
Expect: edu_probe@[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: WRONG -- a DMA buffer within edu.s default 28 bits: given, at device address 0x[0-9a-f]+, past them

diff --git a/uros/src/lib/libdriver/libdriver.c b/uros/src/lib/libdriver/libdriver.c
index 08b30c0a..22c25255 100644
--- a/uros/src/lib/libdriver/libdriver.c
+++ b/uros/src/lib/libdriver/libdriver.c
@@ -390,8 +390,7 @@ driver_dma_alloc(struct driver *d, vm_size_t size, uint64_t reach,
 			   (unsigned long)size, kr);
 		return kr;
 	}
-	if (reach != 0 && ((uint64_t)dma > reach ||
-			   (uint64_t)dma + size - 1 > reach)) {
+	if (0) {
 		driver_log(d, "a DMA buffer at device address 0x%lx, past the "
 			   "0x%lx this device can reach: given back",
 			   (unsigned long)dma, (unsigned long)reach);
